id: divine-healing
name: Divine Healing
type: counter
actionCost: 2
kiCostPerBaseTier: 2
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
usageLimit: 1/round
# A Domain Maneuver (God of a Domain (3)), a God Maneuver: open while the Domain in brackets is yours, only in God Ki, paid in Divine Ki Points.
godManeuver: true
afterDamage: true
# Offered on an attack's card once its Damage is taken (chat.mjs offerDomainAfterDamage), used out of sequence.
source: Core Rule
description: >
  You recover your stamina even as you are being struck, healing yourself with divine grace.
text: >
  Divine Healing [1/Round]: You recover your stamina even as you are being struck, healing yourself with divine grace.
  –Maneuver Type: Counter
  –Action Cost: 2 Counter Actions
  –Minions: N/A
  –DKP Cost: 2(bT)
  –Effect: If you are hit by an Attacking Maneuver and take Damage, you may use this Maneuver. Regain 2d10(bT) Life Points, increasing the Dice Score by your Surgency. This effect is considered a use of Combat Recovery for all of your effects.

---

[on used]
divineHealing();
